    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels like a bridge between abstract thought and tangible problem-solving—something I engage with deeply when it aligns with my creative or analytical interests. It’s not just numbers; it’s about patterns, logic, and the way equations can describe real-world phenomena. Though I find some concepts challenging, especially in physics, I enjoy exploring them as a puzzle to solve, much like how I approach art or literature.",
