    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "Not directly for math, but I’ve used AI tools like translation apps or creative writing prompts (since my PhD involved interdisciplinary research). For pure math, I’d imagine something like Wolfram Alpha or symbolic solvers could help visualize steps—though I’d prefer human guidance to avoid dependency. My extraversion might make me enjoy collaborative problem-solving more than solo digital work.",
